# Tutorials. Each story is one page that a developer follows at the command line.

Story: Your first league run
  As a developer of the executor
  I want to run the league once
  So that I see how it scores and keeps a better executor

  You play one game in the fast arena, then many, to see how fast the arena is. Then you run
  one generation of the league. The league writes down each challenger, a report of the
  generation and the champion.

  Scenario: One game, 64 games, one generation
    Given the league is new
    When the arena plays a game with the default executor
    Then the length of the game is 120 s
    When the arena plays 64 games with the default executor
    Then the speed of the arena is at least 200 times real time
    When the league runs one generation with the evolution strategy
    Then the challengers in the history are 8
    And the report of the generation is written
    And the champion file is written

Story: Judging a Towers captain
  As a developer of a commander for Towers
  I want the league to judge my captain
  So that I know if it is better than the champion

  A captain is a computer commander of Towers. You play one game between two default
  captains. Next, you let the default captain play itself, to see that the two sides are fair.
  Last, you judge the default captain against a timid champion.

  Scenario: One game, a fair test, a judgement
    Given the champion captain is the timid captain
    And the challenger captain is the default captain
    When the arena plays a game of Towers between two default captains
    Then the drones that flew in the captain game are 10
    When the default captain plays itself from both sides
    Then the score of the captain against itself is 0
    When the league judges the captain challenger
    Then the verdict is promoted
